 "recovery_release": {
  "rule": "knight.gd: every strike gives the axe arm (RightShoulder..RightHand + weapon_r) back to the guard pose from the end of its active swing, over 0.08 s eased, inside the one-shot (rel_<key> Blend2 between the strike clip and its one-shot). Per-clip swing end in character.json strike_release.at_s; guard_throughout for a strike whose swing is not the axe's (the shield bash).",
  "at_s": {
   "attack": 0.75,
   "chop_overhead_92": 0.578
  },
  "why_0_75_not_0_72": "the coordinator named 0.72-0.80 s; the slash's active swing ends at 0.750 s (its last frame at >= 50% of peak head speed), so the release starts there and the swing is untouched: through the tree the head and the edge match the raw clip to 0.0000 m and 0.00 deg over all 5 swing frames. The swing mean reads 0.97 (raw 1.00) only because the travel at the swing's last frame is a central difference that reaches the first released frame.",
  "held_pose_note": "the guard pose is played as a copy of the strike's own length, synced: a Blend2 reports the time left of whichever input weighs more than half, and with the pose's 1-frame clip the slash's one-shot ended when the release passed 0.5 (measured: at 0.79 s of 1.50)",
  "slash": "0 of 36 frames through the tree (t = 0.042-1.500 s; the 37th raw frame, t = 0, is the fade-in's start with the strike at weight 0)",
  "bash": {
   "clip_owns_the_arm": "45 of 59 frames (worst 1252 points, 0.44 m)",
   "guard_throughout (staged)": "10 of 58 frames through the tree, worst 41 points 0.12 m: the butt end in his right thigh at the bash's lunge (0.63-1.00 s)",
   "block_guard_throughout": "36 of 59 frames (worst 43) -- not taken",
   "status": "NOT in the acceptance; improved, still FAILS PEN; a bash-specific guard (IK at the bash's chest, like the block's) is the next step"
  }
 },
